   "text": "I read the drawing as a macrocyclic ester/amide built from these pieces, and wrote the SMILES from them.\n\n- **Piperazic acid ring:** a six-membered ring with an N\u2013N bond. The acylated N sits at top right, the NH at lower left, and three CH2 groups complete the ring. The ring carbon next to the NH carries the ester carbonyl and is (S).\n- **Amino-acid linker:** an (S) CH bearing the urea NH, with a CH2 leading to C2 of a thiazole. The CH is acylated onto the piperazic N.\n- **Thiazole:** C4 is attached to C5 of the indole.\n- **Indole:**\n  - N1 carries CH2CF3.\n  - C2 carries the pyridine.\n  - C3 carries CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2\u2013O, which closes the macrocycle as an ester onto the piperazic acid carbonyl.\n- **Pyridine:**\n  - C2 carries the (S) CH(CH3)OMe group.\n  - C3 is bonded to the indole.\n  - C5 carries the N of a bicyclic octahydropyrazino-oxazine, whose bridgehead CH is (S).\n- **Urea:** a (2S)-2,4-dimethylpiperazine joined to the urea carbonyl through N1.\n\nI assigned CIP priorities at each of the five stereocentres and set the @/@@ tags to give S for all of them. For the piperazic carbon, the hashed carbonyl bond puts H toward the viewer, which also gives S and matches the drawn label.\n\nSMILES: O=C9OCC(C)(C)Cc2c(-c3cc(N4CCN5CCOC[C@@H]5C4)cnc3[C@H](C)OC)n(CC(F)(F)F)c3ccc(cc23)-c2csc(n2)C[C@H](NC(=O)N2CCN(C)C[C@@H]2C)C(=O)N2CCC[C@@H]9N2"
